WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.109 --> 00:00:06.109
For generations, the automobile was defined by one thing: the ground beneath it.

2
00:00:06.209 --> 00:00:12.409
Then, in October twenty twenty-six, a demonstration challenged that expectation.

3
00:00:12.484 --> 00:00:16.959
The Roadster performed extraordinary short airborne maneuvers.

4
00:00:17.154 --> 00:00:20.835
The important question is not simply whether it left the ground.

5
00:00:21.348 --> 00:00:27.763
It is how force, engineering, and control made those moments possible—and why a stunt

6
00:00:27.813 --> 00:00:30.988
is not the same thing as sustained flight.

7
00:00:31.088 --> 00:00:33.363
A brief airborne maneuver can look like a revolution.

8
00:00:33.413 --> 00:00:39.737
But the engineering standard is much higher than leaving the ground for a few seconds.

9
00:00:40.196 --> 00:00:45.696
Sustained, controlled flight needs safe and repeatable support of the vehicle’s

10
00:00:45.796 --> 00:00:49.816
weight, stable control, and a practical energy supply.

11
00:00:49.916 --> 00:00:55.211
A powerful demonstration can inspire questions without answering all of them.

12
00:00:55.500 --> 00:01:01.650
The public can observe motion, orientation and the apparent sequence of a

13
00:01:01.750 --> 00:01:07.625
demonstration. It cannot reliably infer hidden plumbing, tank dimensions, exact thrust

14
00:01:07.725 --> 00:01:10.922
or software control laws from a promotional video.

15
00:01:11.286 --> 00:01:16.111
We therefore separate published statements, independent reporting and our own

16
00:01:16.186 --> 00:01:22.986
explanatory drawings. Every flying machine must deal with three intertwined problems:

17
00:01:23.086 --> 00:01:29.361
generate the forces required for motion, control its attitude while those forces act,

18
00:01:29.486 --> 00:01:31.839
and manage the limited energy available.

19
00:01:32.286 --> 00:01:38.261
Those problems will guide our investigation, from the body shape to the mathematics of

20
00:01:38.336 --> 00:01:38.847
hover.
